{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a dual visible-light/cobalt catalytic system for the controllable isomerization of alkenes. By varying the phosphine ligand, the authors achieved either thermodynamic isomerization to the most stable conjugated isomers (using Xantphos) or kinetic isomerization over a single carbon position (using DPEphos). The reaction is accelerated by the donor-acceptor photocatalyst 4CzIPN and utilizes Hantzsch ester as a reductant to generate active cobalt-hydride species.",
